178.
Powers of Central Commission to make regulations.?
(1)
The Central Commission may, by notification make regulations consistent with this Act and the rules generally to carry
out the provisions of this Act.
(2)
In particular and without prejudice to the generality of the power contained in sub-section (1), such regulations may
provide for all or any of following matters, namely:?
